Give each world its own deadline and answers (#1)
The deadline was one module-level variable that each new world reset, so
a world stayed bounded only until another was made. realWorld() now builds
the git and GitHub adapters afresh, closed over their own deadline and
their own caches, so one call's answers never outlive it either.

